---
config:
  sequence:
    mirrorActors: false
    actorMargin: 40
    width: 160
    height: 50
    messageMargin: 26
    boxMargin: 8
    noteMargin: 8
    messageFontSize: 15
    noteFontSize: 14
    actorFontSize: 15
    wrap: false
---
sequenceDiagram
    participant AM as Alice main thread<br/>(login_cli)
    participant AR as Alice reader<br/>lanlink-client-reader
    participant SW as Server worker<br/>lanlink-‹id› (Alice)
    participant SA as Server main thread<br/>(serve_forever)

    AM->>SA: TCP connect (open_connection)
    alt fewer than max_clients (64)
        SA->>SW: start _serve_client
    else server full
        SA--xAM: accept(), then close()
    end
    Note over AM,SW: TLS only (client --cafile, server --cert): handshake in open_connection<br/>and in the worker (tls.wrap_socket), never in the accept loop.<br/>TLS handshake, then HELLO, each get handshake_timeout (server --timeout, 5 s)

    alt TLS handshake and HELLO each within handshake_timeout
        AM->>SW: HELLO (client_name, client_version)
        SW->>AM: HELLO_ACK (ref_request_id, server_name, limits)
        Note over SW: after accept_hello: HELLO_ACCEPTED,<br/>timeout becomes idle_timeout
    else TLS handshake or HELLO too slow
        SW--xAM: socket closed, no ERROR sent
        Note over AM,AR: EOFError or socket error: CLI prints "Client failed"
    end

    Note over AM: getpass("Password: ")
    AM->>SW: AUTH (username, payload = password)
    alt CredentialStore.verify OK (PBKDF2) and username not online
        Note over SW: _users[username] = UserSession(ip, port)<br/>AUTHENTICATED
        SW->>AM: AUTH_OK (ref_request_id, username)
        Note over SW: auth_ready.set()
    else wrong password / unknown user, or already online
        SW->>AM: ERROR AUTH_FAILED or ALREADY_LOGGED_IN
        Note over AM,AR: authenticate raises LanLinkError, the CLI exits<br/>(server closes after the 3rd AUTH_FAILED)
    end

    AM->>AR: PrivateChatClient(...)<br/>starts reader
    AM->>SW: USER_LIST (empty), queue in _pending[request_id]
    SW->>AR: USER_LIST (ref_request_id,<br/>payload = users JSON)
    AR->>AM: reply put in queue<br/>_pending[ref_request_id]
    Note over AM,AR: print user list, start lanlink-cli-input, "> " prompt
